# Code owners for security-critical admission surfaces.
#
# STATUS: this file is currently INERT. GitHub only requests and requires
# code-owner review when "Require a pull request before merging" with
# "Require review from Code Owners" is enabled in branch protection. As of
# 2026-08-03 `main` has `required_pull_request_reviews: null`, so nothing here
# is enforced. It is recorded now so the intent is explicit and the rule takes
# effect the moment a second maintainer makes required reviews practical.
#
# Do not treat the presence of this file as evidence that these paths are
# reviewed. The enforcing control for the staged-successor path is the
# admission workflow itself, not this file.

# The admission validator decides what may enter the repository. A change here
# changes what every future change is checked against.
/tools/admission_root_v1.py                  @jasonewillis

# The staged successor is pre-authorized replacement bytes for the validator
# above. It is the one file whose contents a later pull request may promote
# into the validator position without matching the current baseline, so it
# carries the validator's authority one revision early. It is deliberately
# listed even though it does not exist yet: it must be owned from the moment
# it is first created, not after.
/tools/admission_root_next_v1.py             @jasonewillis

# The workflow that supplies base-owned authority values to the validator.
/.github/workflows/candidate-admission.yml   @jasonewillis

# The declaration that binds tracked sources to their digests.
/.github/admission/v1/source-declaration.json @jasonewillis
